ected past month. Unit Rates for This Month opens the same group and month; save the historical subtotal and return to Invoices to review it. Members retain their existing talk access. Received talks open at the latest post; scroll up to view older posts. Participating Groups lists LINE groups whose join events or posts were received by the official account. New join events and posts add groups automatically. Reload to check participation for groups with earlier received records. Groups without a received record need their next post to be received. Only the master administrator can view unlinked groups. Use Add LINE Talk when creating a normal SKO group or from its participants screen, then choose from the same list. Site, open and partner-company chats are excluded. Members of the linked SKO group can open the original received messages using the LINE group name. Messages are not copied, and The saved received-talk view is read-only; new shared-chat text can be sent to LINE. Linked viewing does not grant attendance or invoice management permissions. Administrators can also use the existing 15-minute connection-code flow. Saved received messages remain after stopping the connection. Earlier unreceived posts and attachments are not imported. Master-only historical aggregation separates unique people and total person-days. Review frozen historical rates, work, overtime and allowances, then explicitly choose the customer, tax and statutory welfare settings to create an invoice draft. Current rates are not automatically applied to history. Existing attendance and invoice approval permissions remain unchanged. After creating an ordinary group, add LINE from Talk functions (︙) or Group settings. The existing group keeps its name, photo and members. Invoices and Unit Rates are opened inside Master Access. Monthly Table provides month swiping, manual row corrections and reimport of received chat and TXT or ZIP data. Save input before switching months. Select one exported text file to save and reimport 33 monthly drafts from January 2024 through September 2026. Review each month's table, save official site names and daily, overtime, early-work and allowance rates with that month, then create a draft using the existing invoice form. Linked LINE posts are also read when a monthly table opens. In addition to the original 33 months, later months through the current month can be supplemented from a UTF-8 TXT file or a ZIP containing one history text, up to 5 MB. Supplement mode retains saved history. An unambiguous received/exported copy becomes one table row while retaining both sources and existing corrections. Ambiguous duplicates require review. Months without incoming posts are unchanged. Explicit month replacement retains received posts. Refresh and save candidates, then review each month before invoicing.",
